@startuml
!theme plain
autonumber

' === Styling ===
skinparam sequence {
  GroupBorderColor black
  GroupFontColor black
  GroupFontSize 12
  BoxPadding 15
  LifeLineBorderColor black
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #f2f2f2
}

' Color lifelines by domain
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor<<Sentry>> #d0e6ff
  BackgroundColor<<FRIDA>>  #ffe5cc
  BackgroundColor<<App>>    #e8e8e8
  BackgroundColor<<User>>   #ffffff
}

actor Bobby as User <<User>>
participant JPMDB as "JPMDB App" <<App>>
participant LAPI as "Sentry Login API" <<Sentry>>
participant STS as "Sentry Token Service" <<Sentry>>
participant FRS as "ForgeRock SaaS" <<FRIDA>>
participant SIDP as "IDA Identity Provider" <<FRIDA>>
participant EA as "Entitlement API" <<Sentry>>
participant DS as "Directory Service" <<Sentry>>
participant HIS as "Human Identity Service" <<Sentry>>
participant KS as "KeyStore" <<Sentry>>
participant AS as "Authorization Server" <<Sentry>>
participant EC as "Entitlement Cache" <<Sentry>>

== 0. Key Exchange & Setup ==
AS -> KS: Request signing keys
activate KS
KS --> AS: Return signing keys
deactivate KS

STS -> KS: Request signing keys
activate KS
KS --> STS: Return signing keys
deactivate KS

STS -> EA: Request EA public keys
activate EA
EA -> STS: Return EA public keys
deactivate EA

JPMDB -> STS: Request Sentry public keys
activate JPMDB
STS --> JPMDB: Return Sentry public keys
deactivate JPMDB

EA -> STS: Request Sentry public keys
activate EA
STS --> EA: Return Sentry public keys
deactivate EA

SIDP -> STS: Request Sentry public keys
activate SIDP
STS --> SIDP: Return Sentry public keys
deactivate SIDP

== 1. Authorization Request (PKCE) ==
group First OIDC Flow: Sentry & JPMDB App
note over User, LAPI
<b>OIDC Authorization Code Flow between JPMDB App and Sentry</b>
end note

User -> JPMDB: Access app
activate JPMDB
JPMDB -> JPMDB: Generate PKCE verifier & code_challenge
JPMDB -> User: Redirect to /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
deactivate JPMDB

note right of User
<b>Bobby is redirected to Sentry for secure OAuth2 login.</b>
end note

User -> LAPI: GET /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
activate LAPI
LAPI -> STS: Forward /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
activate STS
STS -> FRS: Forward /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
activate FRS

note right of FRS
<b>FRS checks if Bobby needs IDA authentication.</b><br>
FR will get the custom_redirect_uri from its agent configuration.<br>
Agent name is the client_id.
end note

FRS -> STS: Redirect to /authorize?idp=ida&client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
deactivate FRS
STS -> LAPI: Redirect to /authorize?idp=ida&client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
deactivate STS
LAPI -> User: Redirect to /authorize?idp=ida&client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
deactivate LAPI

== 2. Federation & Authentication ==
group Second OIDC Flow: FR SaaS & IDA
note over FRS, SIDP
<b>OIDC Authorization Code Flow between FR SaaS and IDA</b>
end note

User -> LAPI: GET /authorize?idp=ida&client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
activate LAPI
LAPI -> FRS: Start federation journey
deactivate LAPI
activate FRS

FRS -> FRS: Generate JWT (AuthID), Sentry PKCE verifier & challenge
FRS -> User: Redirect to IDA /authorize?client_id&Sentry_code_challenge&state&scope&jwt_assertion
deactivate FRS

note right of User
<b>Bobby authenticates with IDA.</b>
end note

User -> SIDP: GET /authorize?client_id&Sentry_code_challenge&state&scope&jwt_assertion
activate SIDP
SIDP -> User: Prompt for credentials
User -> SIDP: POST /authenticate (User ID, Password)
SIDP <-> User: IDA session created
User -> SIDP: GET /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope&jwt_assertion
SIDP -> SIDP: Verify JWT assertion
SIDP -> User: Redirect to Sentry /authorize?code&state
note right of User
<b>IDA returns authorization code.</b>
end note
deactivate SIDP

== 3. Federation Token Exchange & User Profile ==
User -> LAPI: Redirect to /authorize?code&state
activate LAPI
LAPI -> FRS: Continue federation journey
activate FRS

FRS -> SIDP: POST /token (code, Sentry_code_verifier)
activate SIDP
SIDP -> SIDP: Verify PKCE
note right of SIDP
<b>Code verifier matches code challenge.</b>
end note
SIDP --> FRS: Return access_token, id_token, refresh_token
deactivate SIDP
end group
note right of FRS
<b>FRS normalizes user details and updates profile.</b>
end note

FRS -> DS: Update identity shadow data + scopes
activate DS
DS -> HIS: Update identity shadow data + scopes
activate HIS
HIS -> DS: Return identity data
deactivate HIS
DS --> FRS: Return identity data
deactivate DS

FRS -> FRS: Create session cookie
FRS -> LAPI: Return success, redirect to /authorize
deactivate FRS
LAPI -> User: Return success, redirect to /authorize
deactivate LAPI

note right of User
<b>Starting Sentry OIDC flow for Banking App access.</b>
end note

== 4. Authorization Code Grant (PKCE) ==
User -> LAPI: GET /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
activate LAPI
LAPI -> STS: Forward /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
activate STS
STS -> FRS: Forward /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
activate FRS
FRS -> STS: Return /authorize?code&state
deactivate FRS

STS -> EC: Store scopes for code
activate EC
EC -> STS: Success
deactivate EC

STS -> LAPI: Return /authorize?code&state
deactivate STS
LAPI -> User: Redirect to JPMDB /authorize?code&state
deactivate LAPI

User -> JPMDB: Redirect to /authorize?code&state
activate JPMDB

== 5. Token Exchange & Resource Access ==
JPMDB -> LAPI: POST /token (code, code_verifier)
activate LAPI
LAPI -> STS: POST /token (code, code_verifier)
activate STS
STS -> FRS: Validate session, PKCE, generate token
activate FRS
FRS -> STS: Return access_token (aal=1)
deactivate FRS

STS -> EC: Request scopes for code
activate EC
EC -> STS: Return stored scopes
deactivate EC

STS -> EA: TokenExchange with scopes
activate EA
EA -> EA: Validate Bobby's entitlement (simulate Sarah)
EA -> EA: Switch Bobby with Sarah for sub in token
EA -> STS: Return EA token (sub=Sarah)
deactivate EA

STS -> LAPI: Return access_token (aal=1)
deactivate STS
end group
LAPI -> JPMDB: Return access_token
deactivate LAPI

JPMDB -> JPMDB: Verify access_token, show protected page
JPMDB -> User: Present protected content
deactivate JPMDB
deactivate User
@enduml